answers=[
('Were all thirteen numerical references verified?','Yes. Original canonical and qualified M2 packages have exact IDs, XYZ, T0 areas and T2 equality. Triangle-area reconstruction and original region-label rules pass. Fresh full manifested release audits cover R8-E16, R1 and R2.'),
('Were predictions unchanged?','Yes. All 299 available original registered prediction files pass SHA-256 and support verification. No prediction, checkpoint or target is overwritten. B0/B1 have FULL results only; missing restricted fields are not invented.'),
('Was historical High95 exactly reproduced?','Yes. All 299 original source IoU values were recovered before sealing; the independent checker also exactly matches historical binary masks and the new implementation retains High95 separately from rank budgets.'),
('How do N1/N2/N3 perform at each budget?','The complete nine context/budget macro rows are in N3_N2_THRESHOLD_SUMMARY.csv and manuscript Table 6. FULL rank IoUs at 1/5/10% are N1 0.191305/0.649869/0.676745, N2 0.139353/0.548051/0.583907 and N3 0.140055/0.601118/0.605041. Source, plate and seed rows are all retained.'),
('Does N3 improve over N2 at all levels?','All nine rank-budget mean contrasts are positive, but 1% is seed dependent and 10% X43 is adverse under the second seed. Common FE-threshold 1% contrasts are adverse under every context and both seeds. A universal robustness claim is unsupported.'),
('Do improvements hold across all plates?','No. At rank 1%, E and G are adverse under all contexts; at rank 10%, E is adverse under all contexts and C under restricted views. At rank 5%, X is adverse under every context. These post-development contrasts are descriptive.'),
('Does X remain unfavorable?','At 5% relative rank, yes. At 10% rank it becomes favorable; restricted 1% rank is favorable while FULL 1% remains adverse. Common FE 95th-percentile contrasts are favorable in X under all contexts. Its conclusion depends on hotspot definition.'),
('Does ranking change under common FE thresholds?','Yes. N3-minus-N2 mean IoU at common top1% thresholds is −0.06607/−0.05010/−0.03894 under FULL/X50/X43. Common top5% instead favors N3, including all mean plates. N1/N3 FULL top5% order also changes. These reference-derived MPa thresholds are diagnostic only, not deployment inputs.'),
('How sensitive are ties?','For neural fields, source-level 5% rank-versus-historical IoU changes by at most 0.00090120; macro differences are below 0.00015. Nonconstant rank-mask quota deviations are at most 0.001835 percentage points. Constant-baseline rank masks are arbitrary ID ordering and its historical all-high mask is retained. These effects do not explain the common-threshold reversal.'),
('How much core area does G0 cover?','Equal-plate mean 9.5632%, with source range 5.3699–11.2712%. This is broader than the 1% and 5% neural rank budgets and varies by source.'),
('How much reference area does G0 capture?','Mean rank-reference recall is 98.7110%, 87.3770% and 66.1879% at 1/5/10%. At 5% source capture ranges from 64.8981% to 100%. These are rank-budget values, distinct from the preserved original R2 own-CDF High95 fractions.'),
('What are G0 precision, recall and IoU?','At 1%: precision 0.109405, recall 0.987110, IoU 0.109251. At 5%: 0.487918, 0.873770 and 0.461345. At 10%: 0.710418, 0.661879 and 0.522172. Each is an equal-plate mean of source metrics, not a ratio of macro sums. Unequal candidate areas prohibit treating this as an equal-budget contest.'),
('How does G1 compare?','FULL G1 IoUs are 0/0.032933/0.156313 at 1/5/10%; N3 gives 0.140055/0.601118/0.605041. Every one of 78 N3 source/seed/budget comparisons exceeds G1. Other frozen regressors/neural models are retained in the paired CSV, without assigning G1 an MPa field or L2.'),
('Is G1 truly geometry only?','Yes. Its sealed score uses original XYZ, triangle connectivity and the frozen parent-normal relief contour at 0.5 mm. Every component is retained; exact XY segment distances determine rank. No stress, prediction, error, hotspot mask, tuned kernel or alternative contour is used. Independent contour reconstruction checks all thirteen scores.'),
('Is G1 comparable under restricted views?','Not established. The historical parent plane and labels require full-source support. No qualified strictly visible plane/label rule exists. A replacement fit would change the frozen baseline rule, so restricted rows are explicitly NOT_EVALUABLE.'),
('Which comparisons are FULL only?','All direct G0/G1 versus saved-model comparisons. Fifty-two source/model/restricted-context rows record unavailability, with all 34,200 queries marked unqualified for that information contract rather than falsely claimed geometrically absent. Neural-versus-neural restricted comparisons remain valid on unchanged support.'),
('Does neural localization add information beyond collar membership?','For the sealed FULL G1 score, yes; N3 wins at every prescribed source/seed/budget comparison. G0 is already informative at broad recall but has a larger candidate area. The result supports this limited numerical added value, not neural indispensability or superiority to every geometric rule.'),
('Is the added value consistent across sources and plates?','Against this G1, yes for N3 on all 78 FULL comparisons and all fifteen plate/budget means. It does not establish a partial-view baseline comparison. N3-versus-N2 utility remains heterogeneous across plates, seeds, thresholds and regions.'),
('Where do largest weighted errors occur?','Macro weighted SSE is largest in the height region for every neural model/context. Among N3 region rows the largest retained SSE is G07/FULL/seed20261022/HEIGHT_REGION, 178741.983510 MPa² mm². This descriptive within-cohort magnitude is not a fatigue-critical location or a physical validation result.'),
('Which region contributes most?','The height proxy, occupying 80.9572% mean core area, dominates neural macro squared-error contribution. N3 height shares are 46.72–52.93%, parent 24.57–29.09%, and collar the remainder. Lower region MAE can coexist with a larger total share because area differs.'),
('Are collar errors smaller than parent errors?','It depends on model/context. FULL N1 collar/parent MAE is 15.84970/9.79237 MPa; N2 19.18849/17.72843; N3 17.39336/20.67217. N3 therefore reverses the aggregate collar-versus-parent ordering; plate/source/seed rows show heterogeneity.'),
('Does N3 consistently improve any region?','No region improves in every plate/context cell. FULL mean collar MAE improves in all five plates; restricted G worsens, and E also worsens at X50. Height and parent show opposing plate/context changes. REGIONAL_LOWEST_MAE_MODELS.csv identifies the lowest error among every available frozen model.'),
('Why do X10 and X23 respond differently?','The fields show different regional bias and high-set redistribution, but no unique cause is established. X10 has stronger N3 parent underprediction and height overprediction; X23 has different collar and maximum-amplitude behavior. These numerical patterns do not identify a physical geometric defect or isolate learned mechanisms causally.'),
('Which patterns lack a causal explanation?','Source-dependent mask shifts, centroid/IoU disagreement, stronger N3 parent underprediction, height overprediction, and some core-edge error enrichment. Native loading caps, gauges, core edges, owning observation edges and geometric proxy contours are distinct. No independent physical toe trajectory is available.'),
('Are peak amplitudes consistent with overlap gains?','No general consistency follows. Historical N3 peak-amplitude error worsens despite better aggregate High95. Its common extreme-threshold recall is poor, while rank overlap can improve. Relative ranking, field maxima, Q95 amplitudes and threshold classification remain separate quantities.'),
('Were unfavorable findings retained?','Yes. Adverse plates/seeds, common extreme-threshold losses, parent errors, G1 weakness, unequal G0 area, constant-score degeneracy, empty-mask undefined metrics and unavailable partial geometry comparisons are explicit. The initial independent-checker discrepancy and corrected full recheck are preserved.'),
('Were all original plate groups preserved?','Yes: C={C02,C05,C16}, E={E21}, G={G04,G07,G08,G16,G25}, H={H12,H19}, X={X10,X23}; all retain V1-S355-AW identities. Documentary groups are not certified independent manufacturing batches.'),
('Were both seeds retained?','Yes, 20261021 and 20261022. Metrics are scored separately and averaged after the source/plate hierarchy. No favorable seed or prediction ensemble is selected.'),
('Were new FE solves performed?','No. New ANSYS solves, meshes and FE targets all equal zero.'),
('Were any models fitted or re-inferred?','No. Neural training/inference, fine-tuning, XGBoost fitting and other predictive fits all equal zero. Geometry-only deterministic masks are explicitly authorized retrospective comparisons, not new trained models.'),
('Were original targets, IDs or geometry changed?','No. All original arrays and historical releases remain unchanged; new derived tables, masks, geometric scores, plots and manuscripts reside only in the versioned R2.1 workspace.'),
('Are metrics independently reproducible?','Yes. The independent implementation passes 49,065 numerical cells, including 11,676 aggregation cells, and exact rank/common/historical binary masks. Another 8,094 boundary/geometry/grouping cells pass. Independent contour distances agree to 3.20e−14 mm. This is numerical verification of frozen outputs, not independent generalization validation.'),
('Does practical interpretation change?','It narrows: relative 5% success cannot be treated as extreme-amplitude accuracy or uniform plate/region robustness. The matched FULL G1 comparison supports additional numerical information over that one rule, while partial geometry comparisons remain unavailable. Engineering acceptance, deployment and grinding decisions are not established.'),
('Does METHOD_IMPROVEMENT_MIXED remain applicable?','Yes. The original N3/N2 experiment and decision are unchanged. R2.1 qualifies interpretation without rewriting historical results.'),
('Is the final manuscript internally consistent?','The final English paper retains original results, title and verified references, adds explicit retrospective methods/results, preserves nine main figures and moves detailed grids to supplementary files. Final render and consistency checks are documented in MANUSCRIPT_FINAL_QUALITY_AUDIT.md.'),
('Are claims auditable?','The R2.1 claim ledger links numerical claims to source/plate/macro CSV row keys, full numeric payloads and SHA-256. Original claims remain in the preserved R2 ledger. Protocol, input hashes, field registry, scripts and independent receipts are included; large original research binaries remain at their recorded unchanged paths.'),
('Which physical limitations remain?','Processed-scan smoothing and raw registration uncertainty; no authenticated registered toe truth or validated notch radii; assumed planar rear, material, thickness and loading; unresolved nonlocal boundary influence; two-level numerical rather than physical FE validation; no residual stress, plasticity, crack growth, experimental stress measurement or fatigue-life validation; no untouched external cohort.'),
('Is it ready for authors and a target journal?','Ready for final human author review within the verified scope, subject to the completed final Word render/integrity receipt. Target-journal length/style, authorship, public code/data deposition and submission remain author decisions. Acceptance is not guaranteed.'),
('Is the research closed?','Yes. This is the final bounded retrospective assessment. CURRENT_WELDSTRESS_AI_MANUSCRIPT_RESEARCH_CLOSED is issued after closeout. No R8-E17, R2.2, new configuration, model-development campaign or additional optimization is initiated.')]
